00:02:29.573 --> 00:02:30.540
You see those numbers there

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:31.740
on the left side of your screen?

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:35.350
Those are going high above 10%, above 15%.

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:37.350
Then you see us come down.

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:39.450
And the big thing about retail sales is

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.820
retail sales don't take inflation

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:42.690
out of the picture.

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:45.090
So as we're seeing inflation come down,

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:47.190
we have seen those retail
sales numbers come down,

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:49.410
and that's what the Federal
Reserve wants to see.

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:51.720
When we talk about a soft landing,

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:52.770
well this is what they wanna see.

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:53.603
They don't wanna see

00:02:53.603 --> 00:02:55.560
those numbers going negative, turning bad,

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:57.000
and then the economy goes lower

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.080
and folks go out of business,

00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.460
they start laying people off.

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:00.293
No, no, no.

00:03:00.293 --> 00:03:01.620
What the Federal Reserve wants to see is

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:03.240
exactly what you're seeing

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:04.200
up there on your screen,

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.300
which is those numbers start to come down,

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:09.030
retail sales start to reduce lower,

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:11.550
you start to see a deceleration

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:13.050
into maybe a slowdown,

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:15.330
and then the economy can
start to pick back up

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:18.030
as we move back towards
two percent inflation.

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:19.290
So you don't really wanna see zero,

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:20.820
you don't really only wanna see negative.

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:22.380
What you wanna see is the number

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:23.723
for June is 1.5%,

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.490
so you've got a 1.5% increase.

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:27.750
Again, it's from that number

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:29.640
on the far left side of your screen.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:32.850
So what we have seen is a small increase

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.380
from a very high number,

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.000
and those base effects are gonna start

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.500
to play a real big role

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:38.430
as we move forward

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:39.420
and as we continue.

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:40.560
Because you see,

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:42.120
as you see there on your screen,

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:42.953
the numbers are lower

00:03:42.953 --> 00:03:44.730
