00:05:10.433 --> 00:05:12.030
or go to the auto mechanic.

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:14.790
We're seeing that really
holding up inflation,

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:16.110
but what you don't want is for it

00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:18.420
to be pushing inflation too high,

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:20.370
which is what we were seeing last year

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:21.690
and earlier in this year,

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:23.430
which is the inflation rate

00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:24.263
and the sales rate.

00:05:24.263 --> 00:05:26.280
Because we know when people
are going out, spending money,

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:27.690
they're buying, buying, buying,

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:29.070
well, we know prices are going up

00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:30.930
and if people are paying
those high prices,

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.790
the prices just continue to escalate,

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:34.410
and that's not what the Fed wants to see,

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:35.910
that's not what you and I wanna see.

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:37.170
Those higher prices?

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:38.003
we don't want that.

00:05:38.003 --> 00:05:39.570
We want inflation to come down

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:41.610
and really get those price increases

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:42.840
more in control,

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:44.310
see that deceleration.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:45.660
One big surprise, I think,

